  "funFact": "The Portuguese man o' war looks like a jellyfish but is not even a single animal — it is a siphonophore, a colony of specialized organisms (zooids) each performing a different function: floating, stinging, digesting, reproducing. It is still a cnidarian like jellyfish, but its colonial nature makes it one of the strangest organisms in the ocean.",
